WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.732 --> 00:00:07.969
This page explains how the whole site works, what belongs on Blackboard, and where the boundaries are.

2
00:00:07.969 --> 00:00:19.067
Skim the cards in order. They cover what stays on Blackboard, what this site never collects or sends, how readings and media are handled, and the site's known limits.

3
00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:30.069
Try the Reading Lens. The Reading Lens button at the top of every page offers text size, spacing, a high-legibility font, page tints, a reading ruler, a magnifier, and read-aloud.

4
00:00:30.069 --> 00:00:41.074
Translate the site if you want another language. Right click the page and choose Translate. It happens in your browser, in more than one hundred languages. Machine translation can miss nuance, so check important passages against the original.

5
00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:49.229
Know where the guide lives. Course Website Instructions in the menu opens the online guide or downloads the PDF copy.

6
00:00:49.229 --> 00:00:58.323
Use Report a problem when something breaks. It is in the menu on every page. Blackboard remains the reliable path to the instructor.

7
00:00:58.323 --> 00:01:07.475
Clear My Work only when you mean it. The button at the bottom wipes everything this site has saved in this browser. There is no undo.

8
00:01:07.475 --> 00:01:18.485
Back up your saved work. The Take your saved work with you box on this page downloads everything you have typed and rated as one file, and restores it on any device. The accessibility statement lives here too.

9
00:01:18.485 --> 00:01:23.996
Nothing on this site is graded. Blackboard is the only official gradebook.

10
00:01:23.996 --> 00:01:28.184
Where next: Head back Home and open the current week.
